{
  "summary": "Overall the UI matches the design spec and scores very high on accessibility (axe: 0, Lighthouse accessibility 98). All screens are present, the theme tokens are used, and most interactive components provide hover/focus states. However the primary flow for adding a mileage entry is broken – the `Mileage` mini‑FAB cannot be located or activated, which prevents users from completing the core “Add mileage” task. Several secondary states required by the spec (error/retry screens, backup passphrase validation, numeric overflow handling, offline message) are missing or incomplete, which leads to degraded usability but does not completely block the main workflow.\n\nFindings:",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/components/ui/FABAdd.tsx",
      "issue": "The Mini FAB for “Mileage” does not expose an accessible label (`accessibilityLabel`) and is not reachable by UI automation. The test suite cannot locate the button, and real users using screen readers or keyboard navigation have no way to discover the mileage action.",
      "fix": "Add `accessibilityLabel=\"Add mileage\"` (and optionally `accessibilityHint`) to the MiniFAB component when it renders the mileage option. Ensure the mini‑FAB is rendered with a visible text label or an accessible tooltip so that both automated tests and assistive technologies can identify it. Verify that the button has a 44 × 44 dp touch area and focus‑visible styling."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/PolicyScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The spec defines an error state with a full‑screen error view and a **Retry** button when storing the policy acceptance fails. The current implementation only shows the agreement screen and loading indicator – no UI for the error case.",
