{
  "summary": "The UI is largely built around the DESIGN.md token system and component library, and most screens are present. However the primary user flow cannot be completed because the Add action (FAB/EmptyState button) is not discoverable by the test harness – it lacks an accessible name and/or a proper test‑id, breaking the core flow. Several secondary states (error & retry views) are missing or incomplete, and a few accessibility details (touch‑target size for MiniFAB, focus‑visible styling, alt text for images, use of hard‑coded colours) do not fully follow the spec. These issues are grouped by severity below.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/components/ui/FABAdd.tsx",
      "issue": "The FAB that opens the mini‑FABs does not have an `accessibilityLabel` or `testID`. The test suite looks for a button labelled “Add” and times out, meaning users of assistive technology also cannot discover the add‑entry action.",
      "fix": "Add `accessibilityLabel=\"Add receipt or mileage\"` (or separate labels for each mini‑FAB) and a stable `testID=\"fab-add\"`. Ensure the mini‑FABs also expose `accessibilityLabel` (e.g. \"Add receipt\", \"Add mileage\")."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/screens/DashboardScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Missing Error state UI. The spec requires a full‑screen error view with a Retry button, but the component only shows a Snackbar on failure and never renders a retry UI, leaving the user without a recoverable path.",
      "fix": "Implement an `ErrorView` component that displays the copy \"Failed to load data. Pull down to retry.\" and a `PrimaryButton` labelled \"Retry\" that re‑fetches the dashboard data."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/PolicyScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Error state (failed to store acceptance) is not implemented – only the default agreement view exists.",
      "fix": "Add a full‑screen error view with the specified copy and a `PrimaryButton` labelled \"Retry\" that re‑attempts storing the acceptance flag."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/ExportScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "During export the UI disables the buttons but does not show an inner `ActivityIndicator` as described in the spec, and the Snackbar on success uses the generic message \"Export ready to share\" instead of the exact copy.",
      "fix": "Wrap the button label with a small `ActivityIndicator` when `exportRunning` is true and use the exact copy \"Export ready to share\" in the Snackbar."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/BackupScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Passphrase modal is missing the rule text \"Passphrase must be at least 12 characters\" above the inputs, and the primary button remains enabled before validation passes.",
      "fix": "Render the rule description component above the passphrase fields and bind the button's `disabled` prop to the validation result."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/MiniFAB.tsx",
      "issue": "Mini‑FAB size is 40 × 40 dp, which is below the required 44 × 44 dp touch target for interactive elements.",
      "fix": "Increase the hit‑area to at least 44 × 44 dp (e.g., by adding a transparent `TouchableOpacity` wrapper) while keeping the visual icon size at 40 dp."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Focus‑visible style is defined only for web (`outline: 2px solid theme.colors.outline`) but native platforms lack a visible focus indicator, violating the spec's visible focus requirement.",
      "fix": "Add a platform‑agnostic focus style using Paper’s `rippleColor` and a visible border/outline when `focused` is true (e.g., via `onFocus`/`onBlur`)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/ReceiptImagePicker.tsx",
      "issue": "Receipt thumbnail images have no `accessibilityLabel` or `alt` text, breaking the rule that images must have descriptive labels.",
      "fix": "Pass `accessibilityLabel=\"Receipt photo\"` (or the actual file name) to the `Image` component."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/EmptyState.tsx",
      "issue": "Some EmptyState instances use hard‑coded colour values (e.g., `color: '#212121'`) instead of `theme.colors.onSurface`. This bypasses the design token system.",
      "fix": "Replace all literal colours with references to `theme.colors` via the Paper theme (e.g., `color={theme.colors.onSurface}`)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/Screen.tsx",
      "issue": "Horizontal padding is set to a constant `16` instead of using the token `theme.spacing * 2`. This creates a layout that could drift from the 8 dp grid.",
      "fix": "Replace the magic number with `paddingHorizontal={theme.spacing * 2}` to stay consistent with the token system."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/ChoiceField.tsx",
      "issue": "SegmentedButtons do not expose an `accessibilityLabel` for each segment; screen readers read only the group label, making it hard to select a specific option.",
      "fix": "Pass `accessibilityLabel` to each button option (e.g., `{ label: 'Expense', accessibilityLabel: 'Expense' }`)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/screens/SettingsScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The Settings error view only uses a `Snackbar` but the spec defines a full‑screen error view with the copy \"Unable to load settings.\". The Snackbar disappears quickly, leaving the user without a persistent error state.",
      "fix": "Add an error view component that displays the message and a Retry button, matching the spec."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/screens/BackupScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "After a successful backup the temporary file is deleted, but the UI does not wait for the deletion to complete before closing the modal, which can cause a race condition on slower devices.",
      "fix": "Await the file deletion promise before dismissing the modal and showing the success Snackbar."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/ScreenHeader.tsx",
      "issue": "The header uses a plain `<View>` with `role=\"banner\"` but does not set `accessibilityRole=\"header\"` for the title text, reducing heading semantics.",
      "fix": "Wrap the title in a `<Text>` component with `accessibilityRole=\"header\"` (or proper heading level via `variant=\"headlineMedium\"`)."
    }
  ]
}

