{
  "summary": "The UI mostly implements the DESIGN.md spec but critical flaws prevent the core user flow. The FAB that launches the receipt/mileage entry cannot be interacted with (high severity) and several secondary states, token usage, and accessibility details are missing or inconsistent (medium/low). Fixing the Add button and aligning the remaining screens with the spec will bring the product to a polished, production‑ready state.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/components/ui/FABAdd.tsx",
      "issue": "The FAB that opens the receipt/mileage mini‑FABs is not discoverable by accessibility queries – it lacks an `accessibilityLabel`/`accessibilityRole=\"button\"` and the test ID used by the UI‑flow test. As a result the primary flow times out when trying to click the \"Add\" button, preventing users from adding any entry.",
      "fix": "Give the FAB a clear `accessibilityLabel=\"Add\"` (or \"Add entry\"), set `accessible={true}` and `accessibilityRole=\"button\"`. Add a stable `testID=\"fab-add\"`. Ensure the mini‑FABs also have proper `accessibilityLabel`s (\"Add receipt\", \"Add mileage\") and visible focus outlines (`outline: 2px solid ${theme.colors.outline}`) for web."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/ReceiptEntryScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "When the user taps **Save receipt**, the spec requires the button label to be hidden and a spinner to appear, but the current implementation keeps the label visible and shows no loading indicator.",
      "fix": "Add a local `saving` state. While `saving` is true render `<ActivityIndicator size=\"small\" />` inside the button and hide the label (`children={saving ? undefined : 'Save receipt'}`). Disable the button during save."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/MileageEntryScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Same missing spinner/label‑hide behavior as ReceiptEntryScreen, breaking consistency with the spec.",
      "fix": "Mirror the fix from ReceiptEntryScreen – show an ActivityIndicator inside the **Save mileage** button and hide its label while the async save is pending."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/PolicyScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The error view text reads “Unable to store acceptance. Please try again.” which deviates from the required copy “Unable to store **your** acceptance. Please try again.”",
      "fix": "Update the string to match the spec exactly, ensuring the word “your” is present."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/SettingsScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Settings load failures only log to console; no Snackbar with the required message “Unable to load settings.” is displayed.",
      "fix": "Wrap the settings fetch in a try/catch and on error call the shared Snackbar component with the exact copy."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Buttons lack a visible focus style on web; when tabbing they receive only the default outline, which does not use the design token colour (`theme.colors.outline`).",
      "fix": "Add a `:focus-visible` style that applies `outline: 2px solid ${theme.colors.outline}; outline-offset: 2px;` and ensure the style is included in `public/theme.css`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/FormField.tsx",
      "issue": "Form fields do not set appropriate `autoComplete` attributes (e.g., amount, date, mileage). The spec calls for autocomplete and keyboard types.",
      "fix": "Prop‑drill an `autoComplete` prop from the screen components to FormField. For numeric fields set `keyboardType=\"numeric\"` and `autoComplete=\"off\"`; for dates use a date picker component that sets `accessibilityLabel` and `autoComplete=\"bday\"` if appropriate."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/BackupPassphraseScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The backup passphrase input lacks a show/hide toggle, violating the sign‑up/sign‑in best‑practice checklist for password fields.",
      "fix": "Add a trailing icon button that toggles `secureTextEntry` on the TextInput, with an accessible label like “Show passphrase” / “Hide passphrase”. Update the IconButton to use the secondary theme colours."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/RestoreScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The passphrase field also lacks a show/hide toggle and does not focus the field automatically on validation error.",
      "fix": "Implement the same show/hide toggle as in the backup screen and, on validation error, call `ref.current?.focus()` for the first invalid field."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/EmptyState.tsx",
      "issue": "The component uses hard‑coded colour hexes (e.g., `#212121` for text) instead of theme tokens, breaching the design‑token rule.",
      "fix": "Replace all colour literals with references to `theme.colors.onSurface` or the appropriate token. Ensure the CSS class uses `color: var(--color-on-surface);`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/ExportScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "When an export is running, the buttons display an internal ActivityIndicator but the surrounding button remains enabled, allowing rapid repeated taps that could trigger duplicate exports.",
      "fix": "Set `disabled={exportRunning}` on both export buttons while `exportRunning` is true, and ensure the spinner replaces the button's label."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/SummaryCard.tsx",
      "issue": "Card elevation is set to 2dp, while the spec defines elevation 1 for all cards.",
      "fix": "Adjust the elevation prop to use `theme.elevation.level1` (or style `elevation: 1`)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/ScreenContainer.tsx",
      "issue": "Horizontal padding is set to 20dp, deviating from the spec’s 16dp (`spacing * 2`).",
      "fix": "Replace the hard‑coded `paddingHorizontal: 20` with `paddingHorizontal: theme.spacing * 2` (i.e., 16dp)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/ScreenHeader.tsx",
      "issue": "Uses `titleLarge` typography for the screen title; the spec requires `headlineMedium` for the main H1.",
      "fix": "Swap the Text variant to `headlineMedium` or explicitly set style `{...theme.typography.headlineMedium}`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/BottomTabBar.tsx",
      "issue": "Icons lack `accessibilityLabel` and rely only on visual label, which can cause screen‑reader confusion.",
      "fix": "Add `accessibilityLabel={route.title}` to each BottomNavigation tab icon."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "public/theme.css",
      "issue": "The CSS file defines colour custom properties but does not expose a variable for `outline` (used for focus rings). As a result focus styles fall back to default browser outline colours.",
      "fix": "Add `--color-outline: #79747E;` to the root selector and use it in focus‑visible styles."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/BackupButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Contains a class name `backup-btn` that is not defined in any stylesheet, leaving the button unstyled on web.",
      "fix": "Either remove the unused class or add the corresponding CSS rule to `public/theme.css`."
    }
  ]
}

